/// Random-AI machines whose complete generated move table and represented
/// command-boundary state are implemented.
///
/// This is deliberately a named, closed widening.  `RANDOM_MOVES` also holds
/// monsters whose move bodies, powers, roster lifecycle, or state machine are
/// incomplete; a future slice must add a kind here only with the same
/// complete-table and encounter-closure audit.
///
/// #2481 slot 1 adds the three kinds that take Python's **plain** uniform
/// branch. `_run_enemy_phase` (frozen Python, deleted #2827) (native `PrepareForNextTurn`)
/// dispatches EXOSKELETON, INKLET,
/// FLYCONID, SLITHERING_STRANGLER, SPECTRAL_KNIGHT, RAT, FABRICATOR and
/// FAKE_MERCHANT_MONSTER to their own advance functions and only *falls
/// through* to `_roll_uniform_cr_intent` for the rest. Membership in
/// `_UNIFORM_CR_ORDER` is therefore **not** the test — Exoskeleton and Inklet
/// are in that table yet are hybrid machines whose non-RAND states follow a
/// fixed successor and spend no `MonsterAi` draw at all. Adding them here on
/// the strength of that table would consume a draw native does not and
/// desynchronise the stream from the first turn (I6). They stay refused.
/// Slot 3 adds the three hybrid machines, each ported from its own Python
/// advance/roll function and its own IL rather than by analogy: Inklet and
/// Exoskeleton return to a fixed successor without spending a draw, and
/// Flyconid's weights are cooldown windows rather than CannotRepeat.
/// Knights elite: FlailKnight::GenerateMoveStateMachine (v111 RVA 0xb47bc)
/// adds WAR_CHANT as CannotRepeat and FLAIL / RAM with maxTimes=2, starting at RAM.
/// SpectralKnight's direct HEX -> SLASH tail is modeled separately in turn.rs.
///
/// #3357 adds the event Mysterious Knight on the same machine.
/// `MysteriousKnight` (v111) is a `FlailKnight` subclass that overrides only
/// `AfterAddedToRoom` (RVA `0xb9fe4`; its type has no other method besides
/// `.ctor` and the base-call thunk `<>n__0` RVA `0xba02f`), so it inherits
/// `FlailKnight::GenerateMoveStateMachine` RVA `0xb47bc` verbatim — the same
/// RAM opener, the same WAR_CHANT CannotRepeat / FLAIL and RAM `maxTimes=2`
/// branches — and every roll is `MonsterModel::RollMove` RVA `0x825c8` over
/// the one shared `RngStream::Ai`, exactly as for the elite Flail Knight. The
/// damage getters are inherited too, which is why the generated
/// `MYSTERIOUS_KNIGHT_*` tiers equal `FLAIL_KNIGHT_*`.
pub const RANDOM_AI_ALLOWLIST: [MonsterKind; 17] = [
    MonsterKind::Exoskeleton,
    MonsterKind::Fabricator,
    MonsterKind::FlailKnight,
    MonsterKind::Flyconid,
    MonsterKind::FossilStalker,
    MonsterKind::HunterKiller,
    MonsterKind::Inklet,
    MonsterKind::LeafSlimeS,
    MonsterKind::Mawler,
    MonsterKind::MysteriousKnight,
    MonsterKind::SlitheringStrangler,
    MonsterKind::SludgeSpinner,
    MonsterKind::SoulNexus,
    MonsterKind::SpectralKnight,
    MonsterKind::TheObscura,
    MonsterKind::TwigSlimeM,
    MonsterKind::TwoTailedRat,
];

/// Whether the cold catalog should compile this random table for execution.
pub(crate) fn random_ai_is_allowlisted(kind: MonsterKind) -> bool {
    RANDOM_AI_ALLOWLIST.contains(&kind)
}

/// Monster kinds whose `Repeats::Fixed` loop successors are admitted.
///
/// The *execution* of a fixed successor is already kind-agnostic (`turn.rs`
/// bounds-checks `next` and assigns `loop_pos`), and so is Python's:
/// `monster_act` (frozen Python, deleted #2827) calls `_resolve_follow`, which returns a
/// non-tuple `follow` unchanged with no kind dispatch. This is
/// therefore an *admission* allowlist, deliberately narrower than the
/// implementation — a kind joins it only once every body in its generated
/// table is implemented, no argument-shape arm rejects its tuples, and it
/// carries no unrepresented kind-private state.
///
/// Because the premise is a property of the **generated** tables, it can be
/// invalidated by a content regeneration rather than by an edit here:
/// `allowlisted_fixed_successor_kinds_have_no_conditional` interrogates the
/// real successor gate against `LOOPS`, so a regenerated `Conditional` that
/// lacks an explicit source-specific arm fails the suite instead of silently
/// taking the generic tail.
/// MagiKnight::GenerateMoveStateMachine (v111 RVA 0xb9264) fixes the loop
/// POWER_SHIELD -> DAMPEN -> RAM -> PREP -> MAGIC_BOMB -> RAM.
/// TrackerRubyRaider::GenerateMoveStateMachine (v111 RVA 0xc3474) builds
/// TRACK_MOVE (IL_0012, `DebuffIntent`) and HOUNDS_MOVE (IL_0038,
/// `MultiAttackIntent(HoundsDamage, HoundsRepeat)`), sets
/// TRACK.FollowUpState = HOUNDS (IL_0069–IL_006b) and
/// HOUNDS.FollowUpState = HOUNDS (IL_0070–IL_0072), and starts on TRACK
/// (IL_0085 `ldloc.1`): TRACK fires once and HOUNDS repeats — the generated
/// `Repeats::Fixed(1)` on HOUNDS_MOVE (#2850). Both bodies are shared
/// registry kinds: `<TrackMove>d__12::MoveNext` (RVA 0x372cec) IL_00a9–IL_00b7
/// `PowerCmd.Apply<FrailPower>(targets, 2, Creature, null, false)` is
/// `frail_player` 2; `<HoundsMove>d__13::MoveNext` (RVA 0x372bd4)
/// IL_0021–IL_0070 `DamageCmd.Attack(HoundsDamage).WithHitCount(HoundsRepeat)`
/// is `attack`.
pub(crate) const FIXED_SUCCESSOR_ALLOWLIST: [MonsterKind; 27] = [
    MonsterKind::Axebot,
    MonsterKind::BowlbugNectar,
    MonsterKind::BygoneEffigy,
    MonsterKind::CalcifiedCultist,
    MonsterKind::CeremonialBeast,
    MonsterKind::CubexConstruct,
    MonsterKind::DampCultist,
    MonsterKind::DevotedSculptor,
    MonsterKind::Fogmog,
    MonsterKind::FrogKnight,
    MonsterKind::HauntedShip,
    MonsterKind::LivingFog,
    MonsterKind::LivingShield,
    MonsterKind::MagiKnight,
    MonsterKind::MechaKnight,
    MonsterKind::Ovicopter,
    MonsterKind::Queen,
    MonsterKind::ScrollOfBiting,
    MonsterKind::ShrinkerBeetle,
    MonsterKind::TheInsatiable,
    MonsterKind::ThievingHopper,
    MonsterKind::TorchHeadAmalgam,
    MonsterKind::TestSubject,
    MonsterKind::ToughEgg,
    MonsterKind::TrackerRubyRaider,
    MonsterKind::Tunneler,
    MonsterKind::WaterfallGiant,
];

