/// with a deterministic HP: 219/209 at A8+, 209/199 below.
/// `monsters::kaiser_roster_is_valid` pins the pair at the fight's ascension
/// (`MONSTER_MODELS`, #2539).
///
/// Until #2539 the pin was the A8+ pair alone, and a `(209, 199)` roster was
/// refused *as a proxy for ascension*: every move constant these two spend is
/// gated one ascension HIGHER — `GetValueIfAscension(9, …)` in
/// `Crusher::get_ThrashDamage` `0xb1e6a` (14/12), `get_BugStingDamage`
/// `0xb1e82` (7/6), `get_AdaptStrengthGain` `0xb1e90` (3/2),
/// `get_GuardedStrikeDamage` `0xb1e9b` (14/12),
/// `Rocket::get_TargetingReticleDamage` `0xbc912` (4/3),
/// `get_PrecisionBeamDamage` `0xbc91d` (20/18), `get_LaserDamage` `0xbc92a`
/// (35/31) and `get_ChargeUpStrengthGain` `0xbc937` (3/2). That proxy never
/// fired on a real root (the oracle built 219/209 for every ascension), and
/// the ascension now reaches `HotState` directly. Since #2828 `LOOPS` carries
/// both tiers of each of those constants and the catalog compiles the fight's
/// (`floor(12 * 3/2) = 18` below A9, where the table alone used to deal
/// `floor(14 * 3/2) = 21`).
///
/// The rage amounts are `CrabRagePower::get_CanonicalVars` `0xa0e0b`:
/// `StrengthPower` 6 then a `BlockVar` of 99.
