/// Exact current-build static-Ethereal Skill/Power rows whose OnPlay program is
/// an ordinary generated body and whose keyword lifecycle is the shared
/// turn-end Ethereal exhaust.
///
/// Current `sts2.dll` SHA-256
/// `9cb4f1ad8c9f284aa8fec3122ffd6d780bbf543d875c817abdd12ff63fbf12b4`:
/// `Defy::get_CanonicalKeywords` RVA `0xdd61c`,
/// `EnfeeblingTouch::get_CanonicalKeywords` RVA `0xde922` and
/// `Demesne::get_CanonicalKeywords` RVA `0xdd7a0` each return the single
/// keyword enum `2` (Ethereal) — no Exhaust, Retain or Sly rides along, and no
/// row here has a `get_HasTurnEndInHandEffect` override, so the shared
/// `_end_player_turn_after_auto_post` (frozen Python, deleted #2827) snapshot-and-exhaust owns the
/// whole keyword lifecycle exactly as it does for the static-Ethereal Attacks
/// above.
///
/// Every body is one ordinary generated program on the already-implemented
/// step vocabulary:
/// - `Defy/<OnPlay>d__9::MoveNext` RVA `0x3982a0` — assert `cardPlay.Target`,
///   presentation `TriggerAnim('Cast')`, `CreatureCmd::GainBlock(Owner.Creature,
///   DynamicVars.Block, card, false)`, then `Apply<WeakPower>(cardPlay.Target,
///   DynamicVars.Weak.BaseValue, Owner.Creature, card, false)`. `.ctor` RVA
///   `0xdd5e3` fixes Energy cost 1 / Skill / Common / `AnyEnemy`;
///   `get_CanonicalVars` RVA `0xdd5f3` fixes Block 6 and Weak 1, and
///   `OnUpgrade` RVA `0xdd697` raises only Block by 3.
/// - `EnfeeblingTouch/<OnPlay>d__8::MoveNext` RVA `0x39bb64` — the identical
///   assert/anim prefix, then one
///   `Apply<EnfeeblingTouchPower>(cardPlay.Target, StrengthLoss.BaseValue,
///   Owner.Creature, card, false)`. That is instruction-for-instruction the
///   already-admitted `DarkShackles/<OnPlay>d__8::MoveNext` RVA `0x396954`
///   shape, and `EnfeeblingTouchPower::.ctor` RVA `0xa20b5`,
///   `DarkShacklesPower::.ctor` RVA `0xa147d` and `ManglePower::.ctor` RVA
///   `0xa491d` all delegate to the same `TemporaryStrengthPower::.ctor` with
///   `get_IsPositive` false, so `TemporaryStrengthPower::get_Sign` RVA
///   `0xa9add` yields `-1` and `get_InternallyAppliedPower` RVA `0xa9ad3`
///   yields `StrengthPower` for all three. `.ctor` RVA `0xde8fe` fixes Energy
///   cost 1 / Skill / Uncommon / `AnyEnemy`; `get_CanonicalVars` RVA `0xde90b`
///   fixes StrengthLoss 8 and `OnUpgrade` RVA `0xde99f` adds 3.
/// - `Demesne/<OnPlay>d__7::MoveNext` RVA `0x3986c0` — presentation
///   `TriggerAnim('PowerUp')`, then `Apply<DemesnePower>(Owner.Creature,
///   DynamicVars.Cards.BaseValue, Owner.Creature, card, false)`. `.ctor` RVA
///   `0xdd774` fixes Energy cost 3 / Power / Rare / `Self`;
///   `get_CanonicalVars` RVA `0xdd781` fixes Energy 1 and Cards 1, and
///   `OnUpgrade` RVA `0xdd803` lowers only the Energy cost by one.
///
/// Registry equality pins every level's complete immutable row, so a mutated
/// keyword, cost or step operand stays a `CardKeyword` refusal. This widens
/// only where the engine looks for the Ethereal lifecycle; it does not relax
/// what the rest of `ordinary` accepts.
/// Parse::get_CanonicalKeywords (v111 RVA 0xe7442) supplies Ethereal;
/// OnPlay MoveNext 0x3b1968 draws CardsVar 3/4 through CardPileCmd::Draw.
fn static_ethereal_body_program_is_supported(row: &CardRow) -> bool {
    if seance_program_is_supported(row) {
        return true;
    }
    matches!(
        (row.id, row.upgrade),
        (
            CardId::Defy | CardId::EnfeeblingTouch | CardId::Demesne | CardId::Parse,
            0 | 1
        )
    ) && crate::content_tables::card_row(row.id, row.upgrade) == Some(row)
}

/// Exact current-build dynamic manual-play predicates owned by the shared
/// play gate.
///
/// Current `sts2.dll` SHA-256
/// `9cb4f1ad8c9f284aa8fec3122ffd6d780bbf543d875c817abdd12ff63fbf12b4`.
/// Grand Finale's `get_IsPlayable` RVA `0xe17eb` reads the owner's live Draw
/// pile and returns true only when its count is zero. High Five's
/// `get_IsPlayable` RVA `0xe29b9` returns exactly `!Owner.IsOstyMissing`, while
/// its body RVA `0x3a592c` independently returns before its attack when Osty
/// is absent. Python `_card_meets_play_condition` (frozen, deleted #2827) preserves both
/// live reads. Native AutoPlay bypasses `CanPlay`, so these are manual-
/// enumeration/direct-play predicates rather than body guards. Registry
/// equality pins all six complete immutable rows; no other textual
/// `play_condition` becomes executable through this carveout.
/// Clash::get_IsPlayable (v111 0xdb093), lambda 0x39256e: every
/// card in the owner's live Hand has CardType.Attack (1).
fn dynamic_play_condition_program_is_supported(row: &CardRow) -> bool {
    matches!(
        (row.id, row.upgrade, row.play_condition),
        (CardId::GrandFinale, 0 | 1, Some("draw_pile_empty"))
            | (CardId::HighFive, 0 | 1, Some("osty_alive"))
            | (CardId::Clash, 0 | 1, Some("all_hand_attacks"))
    ) && crate::content_tables::card_row(row.id, row.upgrade) == Some(row)
}

